# Interview Questions to Remember

### Who recreates a deleted Pod?

ReplicaSet.

### Who manages the ReplicaSet?

Deployment.

### What is maxSurge?

Maximum number of extra Pods allowed above the desired replica count
during a RollingUpdate.

### What is maxUnavailable?

Maximum number of Pods allowed to be unavailable during a RollingUpdate.

### What happens when a new image is deployed?

A new ReplicaSet is created and Pods are gradually replaced according to
the rollout strategy.

### How do you check rollout status?

``` bash
kubectl rollout status deployment <name>
```

### How do you see revision history?

``` bash
kubectl rollout history deployment <name>
```

### How do you roll back to a specific revision?

``` bash
kubectl rollout undo deployment <name> --to-revision=<number>
```

### RollingUpdate vs Recreate?

RollingUpdate gradually replaces Pods; Recreate terminates the old Pods
first and then creates the new Pods.

